{
  "heading": "What a controller method is",
  "body": "A controller method is an instance method with a route annotation, such as `GetRoute`. Your code does not read standard input or write an envelope (the wrapper around the response). It does not declare main, import a Tachyon symbol or extend a framework class. Tachyon does that work. The server answers `OPTIONS` and `HEAD` for you. A request for a verb that no method on that path answers gets 405, with an `Allow` header.\n\nC++ has no tab here, because this example sets its status with `ResponseStatus`, which C++ route controllers do not have yet: the build refuses it in C++ with `TY2015` (ADR 0099).",
